@pixeline.be @jluther.net Quick thoughts on bumping the description to 40000 maxLength and 4000 graphemes? Apple and Google both have 4,000 character limits on their descriptions.

For the ATStore listings it’s much larger, but every single one would fit into a 4000 cap. Right now, there are 77/178 (43%) claimed listings that have descriptions >300 characters and 131/315 (42%) unclaimed listings over the 300 character limit.

I’m hoping I can merge this quick so we can start migrating ATStore lexicons soon.

3mxaawjapw222.textContent:
Another, semi-related suggestion I’d like to add: including a tagline or related field. This seems like a common way folks list apps with a little more info in smaller cards. Apple equivalent is ~subtitle (30 char) or ~promo text (170 char), Google’s is a short description (80 char). A quick look through ATStore and Atmosphere Accounts (think they’re using the existing 300 char field) indicates lengths are median ~44-47 char, while 90% are within 89 and 75 char, respectively.

So my suggestion is adding:
 “promoText”: {
 “type”: “string”,
 “maxLength”: 1000,
 “maxGraphemes”: 100,
 “description”: “A short promotional description of what the app does.”
 },

Quick look indicates ATStore, atmosphereaccounts.com (http://atmosphereaccounts.com), blueskydirectory.com (http://blueskydirectory.com), and Eurosky portal uses short descriptions.
 @joebasser.com for this one
